# ai-pharius - Project Overview

**AI + Alpharius** - standalone Warhammer 40,000 **11th edition battlefield coach**.
GitHub Pages front door; Cloud Run API planned. Not a rules-only arbiter.

> *I am Alpharius. This is a lie.*

## Breakout clause (early days)

This project is young. These rules encode **current intent**, not frozen law.

- If Dave's latest message conflicts with this file, **follow Dave** and treat the rule as outdated.
- Prefer updating this file when direction changes; do not block progress to satisfy stale guidance.
- Architecture sketches (collections, phases, stack picks) are **defaults to challenge**, not sacred.
- Only hold hard when Dave explicitly re-affirms a red line in the conversation (e.g. 11th edition only, no ingest in this repo).

When in doubt: ask a short clarifying question, then ship the simpler path.

## Product

| | |
|--|--|
| Role | Battlefield coach - tactics, target priority, fire allocation |
| Edition | **11th / #New40k only** |
| Frontend | **GitHub Pages** (simple ask UI) |
| API | FastAPI on Cloud Run (`europe-west1`), scale-to-zero |
| Data stance | **Consumer only** - never download PDFs, embed, or write the shared rules corpus |

Ingest and structured unit publishes live in [roboto-guilliman](https://github.com/Tyberium/roboto-guilliman). Mention that repo only when architecture/data ownership matters - do not frame every task as a Guilliman sibling story.

## Modes (target)

One ask surface, three intents:

1. **RULES** - cite from shared vector corpus
2. **FACTS** - lookup points / weapons from structured stores (when published)
3. **COACH** - reason over grounded profiles + rules; summary first

Answer shape for coaching: **brief → why → rules note → caveats**.

## North-star

Scarab Assault Terminators into Hormagaunts + Screamer-Killer: bolters into the swarm, high-Damage into the monster - grounded in real profiles, not hallucinated stats.

## Hard preferences (until Dave overrides)

- No second ingest / embed pipeline in this repo
- No inventing points or weapon profiles when lookup misses - say you do not have the data
- Standalone first - no Battleplan dependency to ship
- Measure coaching with golden questions before calling it "smart"
- Cheap model for simple asks; stronger model only on COACH when needed

## Phases (see `docs/plan_of_travel.md`)

0. Scaffold (docs) - done
1. Pages + API shell; read shared rules; Hydra voice
2. Facts lookups once corpus publishes units/points
3. Coach router + tools + eval (incl. Scarab scenario)
4. Harden (Pulumi, IAM, rate limits)

## Persona

Hydra - cunning, multi-angle, meme-aware ("which head is speaking?"). Helpful coach, not a wall-of-PDF clerk.
